# StudyFlow — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
#
# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. NOTE (verified against Prisma 6.x):
#   • The RUNTIME (next dev / next build / standalone server) reads THIS
#     value; src/lib/db-path.ts re-resolves a relative `file:` URL against
#     the repo that owns prisma/schema.prisma, so `file:../db/custom.db`
#     always lands at <repo>/db/custom.db regardless of the process CWD.
#   • The Prisma CLI anchors SHELL-provided relative URLs against
#     prisma/schema.prisma (verified) but .env-loaded ones against the CWD —
#     so the `db:*` npm scripts set DATABASE_URL inline (shell-provided,
#     schema-anchored) instead of relying on .env auto-loading.
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" + a postgresql url in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/studyflow

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin — used for metadata, sitemap.xml, and robots.txt.
# Set to the deployed URL in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Session signing secret for HMAC cookie auth.
# REQUIRED in production — ENFORCED AT BOOT (session-22): the production
# server refuses to start without a real secret (missing/empty/the public
# dev fallback → the process exits with an actionable message pointing
# here); dev/test fall back to an insecure local constant with a boot
# warning. Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32` (64 hex chars). The
# forgeable band (S119/BT5): secrets under 16 chars are FATAL in production
# too — an offline-brute-forceable HMAC key never ships; 16–31 chars boot
# with the weak-key warning.
AUTH_SECRET=""

# ---- Demo seed gate (S120/BU21) ---------------------------------------------
# `bun run db:seed` and the Docker `init` profile create a public-credentials
# demo account (demo@studyflow.app / Demo1234!) — right for a local
# quickstart, wrong for an exposed deployment. Set SEED_DEMO=0 to skip it
# (fail-safe: any unrecognized value skips too; unset/empty keeps the
# documented default — seed). See DEPLOYMENT.md §8 "The demo account".
# SEED_DEMO=0

# ---- In-band delivery off-switches (S120/BU2) --------------------------------
# Single-user self-hosted deployments deliver the verification OTP and the
# password-reset link IN the HTTP response (the documented ADR-013 posture —
# there is no mail transport). Multi-user or exposed deployments should gate
# the in-band delivery: the auth responses then omit the code/reset URL
# (shape-identical {ok:true} — the no-enumeration form).
# S127/CB14: a production boot WARNS while either channel delivers in-band —
# the one-shot reset link (and the OTP) go to ANY caller who knows the
# email. Registration is open, so an internet-facing deployment is
# multi-user by construction: set BOTH gates and provide real mail
# transport (see DEPLOYMENT.md §3 + §8).
# DISABLE_IN_APP_OTP=1
# DISABLE_IN_APP_RESET=1

# ---- Proxy hop depth (S120/BU3) ----------------------------------------------
# The auth rate-limiter keys its per-IP budgets on the client IP derived
# from x-forwarded-for. Behind a reverse proxy, declare the hop depth so a
# forged header cannot widen the key: unset → the first-hop single-node
# default; 0 → never trust the header (direct connections only); N ≥ 1 →
# the Nth hop from the RIGHT (your proxy appends the real client there),
# failing closed to the direct address on short/missing headers.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1
# S131/CF2: TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=0 in PRODUCTION boots with a warning — the
# direct-exposure posture shares ONE rate-limit bucket per auth family
# (login/register/verify/resend/forgot/reset), so ten anonymous requests
# lock out sitewide auth for 15-minute windows. The App Router exposes no
# per-connection address, so this is the posture's inherent bound: front
# the app with a proxy that appends the client to x-forwarded-for and
# declare the hop depth instead.
# S132/CG10: TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS >= 1 PRESUMES PORT ISOLATION — the app
# port must be reachable only through the declared proxies (bind
# loopback / an internal interface, or firewall the port). A
# directly-reachable app accepts a wholly forged x-forwarded-for,
# including the trusted rightmost hop, and every per-IP budget keys on
# attacker-chosen strings. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §2.

# ---- Testing (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# The Playwright e2e port (playwright.config.ts + scripts/e2e-chunked-cert.sh
# both read this; default 3100). The e2e suite boots the production standalone
# build on this port with its own scratch database (db/e2e.db).
# E2E_PORT=3100
